    "registration": {
      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "HUNG Chün 洪鈞 (T. 陶士, H. 文卿), Jan. 12, 1840–1893, Oct. 2, scholar and diplomat, was a native of Wu-hsien (Soochow). He became a chü-jên in 1864 and four years later a chin-shih (1868), with the highest honors known as chuang-yüan.",
          "source": "eccp-3640788",
          "kind": "source-wording",
